{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And YHWH appeared to him in the terebinths of Mamre.</b> For Abraham was circumcised there at that time, and his entire household was circumcised with him there. The Blessed El caused His Shekhinah to appear to His people in the covenant, as is the practice for all who enter a covenant — as in ״אַתֶּם נִצָּבִים״ (Deuteronomy 29:9–11), and as in ״וַיִּכְרֹת לִפְנֵי ה׳ וַיַּעֲמֹד כָּל הָעָם בַּבְּרִית״ (II Kings 23:3). And it appeared that Abraham was prepared, more than all the others, for that vision. So too the meaning of ״וַיִּפְגְּשֵׁהוּ ה׳״ (Exodus 4:24) — He did not appear there to speak with Moses, but His Shekhinah appeared to receive the covenant of his son, as it says: ״בֵּינִי וּבֵינֵיכֶם לְדוֹרֹתֵיכֶם״ (Genesis 17:12). And perhaps for this reason it became the custom to set a chair at the time of circumcision and in its place."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The verse citation ״אַתֶּם נִצָּבִים״ spans Deuteronomy 29:9–11 in the Hebrew verse numbering (29:10–12 in English); I have followed the Hebrew numbering as Sforno cites it."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:30:32.852939601Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}